cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the software and the associated article described in preferred-citation."

title: "Experimental Platform - LLM-Based Conversational vs Graphical Decision Support"
type: software

# Software authors should reflect contributions to the repository/software itself,
# independently of article authorship.
authors:
  - family-names: "Figliè"
    given-names: "Roberto"
  - family-names: "Caputo"
    given-names: "Simone"


abstract: >-
  Research platform accompanying Figliè et al. (2026), "Neither Replacement nor
  Panacea: Comparing LLM-Based Conversational and Graphical Decision Support in
  Industrial Tasks". It implements the dashboard and conversational conditions,
  shared industrial scenario, study flow, questionnaires, task scoring, and event
  logging used for the study. The repository contains synthetic scenario data and
  experimental materials, but no participant records or original deployment
  credentials.

keywords:
  - human-computer interaction
  - decision support
  - large language models
  - conversational user interfaces
  - dashboards
  - Industry 4.0
  - experimental platform

